CHANGES IN VERSION 0.1.1 (2026-05-13)
-------------------------------------

* HOMER `makeTagDirectory` flags that bam2td does not implement are now
  recognised by the argument parser and skipped with a warning, including
  any value arguments they would consume in HOMER. This lets a user paste
  an existing makeTagDirectory command and have bam2td run with whatever
  it understands, instead of hard-erroring on the first unsupported flag.
  Genuinely unknown flags (not present in HOMER either) still hard-error.

* When `-v` is set, the "Wrote tag directory ..." trailer prints the tag
  count with comma-separated thousands.

* Added a synthetic test suite covering argument handling, SE/PE output,
  per-(pos, strand, length) line splitting, filter flags, strand and
  length transforms, `tagInfo.txt` layout, multi-chromosome behaviour,
  and the new HOMER-flag warn-and-skip path. Runnable via `make test`.


CHANGES IN VERSION 0.1.0 (2026-05-13)
-------------------------------------

* Initial release. Reads coordinate-sorted BAM/SAM/CRAM via htslib and
  writes a HOMER-compatible tag directory (per-chromosome `*.tags.tsv`,
  optional `petag.tsv`, `tagInfo.txt`) that downstream HOMER tools
  consume directly. `chr*.tags.tsv` files are byte-identical to
  `makeTagDirectory` output. `tagInfo.txt` matches HOMER's layout —
  column-header row, summary row, key=value metadata, three-column
  per-chromosome rows, and a `cmd=` trailer — except for the
  autocorrelation-derived `fragmentLengthEstimate` / `peakSizeEstimate`
  values, which require the autocorrelation pass that is not implemented
  in this release. `gsizeEstimate` mirrors HOMER's `appearentSize`
  accounting (sum of the largest emitted tag position per chromosome).

* Supported flags: `-genome`, `-mapq`, `-minlen`, `-maxlen`, `-tbp`,
  `-precision`, `-mis`, `-flip`, `-sspe`, `-single`, `-rmsoft`,
  `-omitSN`, `-keepAll`, `-keepOne`, `-unique`, `-read1`, `-read2`,
  `-keepDup`, `-keepQCfail`, `-p`, `-v`.

* Positional argument order matches HOMER's `makeTagDirectory`:
  `bam2td <output-dir> <input.bam|sam|cram> [options]`.

* When `-v` is set, the program prints elapsed time and peak resident
  memory at the end.

* Build mirrors quaqc: vendored htslib and zlib source trees under
  `libs/` are built as static archives and linked into the binary.
  `make release-full` builds the libraries from source first;
  `hts_dyn=1` / `z_dyn=1` opts into system shared libraries.
